      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.95,
      "end_seconds": 10.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "not at all, please sit. What seems to be wrong?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.24,
      "end_seconds": 18.86,
      "duration_seconds": 6.62,
      "text": "Okay, so so the thing is, I've got not opening my bowels."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.55,
      "end_seconds": 21.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.08,
      "end_seconds": 27.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.85,
      "text": "mm, it's been six months, I'm fairly sure"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.46,
      "end_seconds": 38.69,
      "duration_seconds": 10.23,
      "text": "Yes, carry on. Right, tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.08,
      "end_seconds": 61.43,
      "duration_seconds": 21.35,
      "text": "Prune juice helps a bit. A three out of ten, I suppose. Oh, and hard small stools. That's been about the same, about a year. A bloated tummy was there, um, but it's gone away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.29,
      "end_seconds": 67.19,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "Can I check a a few measurements before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.61,
      "end_seconds": 82.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "Right, that's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.58,
      "end_seconds": 103.97,
      "duration_seconds": 9.39,
      "text": "Okay: SpO2 97 percent on room air, heart rate 84. And respiratory rate 14, temp 36.4 degrees, blood pressure 125 over 78."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.65,
      "end_seconds": 106.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.92,
      "end_seconds": 111.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "I'll interpret them after the the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.77,
      "end_seconds": 117.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "Now I'm going to do a short physical check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.28,
      "end_seconds": 122.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Alright, I'll listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.3,
      "end_seconds": 137.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.96,
      "text": "There is firm stool in the left lower abdomen and no mass."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.51,
      "end_seconds": 142.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.77,
      "text": "please sit back down"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.34,
      "end_seconds": 161.68,
      "duration_seconds": 5.34,
      "text": "Any vomiting, blood in the stool, passing wind or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.15,
      "end_seconds": 171.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "Um, no, none of those at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.65,
      "end_seconds": 177.74,
      "duration_seconds": 5.09,
      "text": "okay, anything with your heart, like skipped beats or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.6,
      "end_seconds": 180.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "nothing like that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.64,
      "end_seconds": 185.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.12,
      "text": "Alright, anything on the skin I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.35,
      "end_seconds": 194.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "right, no, skin's been fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.37,
      "end_seconds": 198.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 199.5,
      "end_seconds": 203.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "Um, no, I've never been operated on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.63,
      "end_seconds": 208.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "alright, have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 210.39,
      "end_seconds": 213.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "I've never had an allergy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.07,
      "end_seconds": 217.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "Do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.54,
      "end_seconds": 231.26,
      "duration_seconds": 8.72,
      "text": "Paracetamol, 650 milligrams, when needed. I'd been on naproxen, not any more though, I stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.65,
      "end_seconds": 236.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 242.16,
      "end_seconds": 255.39,
      "duration_seconds": 13.23,
      "text": "I've had arthritis in my knees for nearly five years now. I looked a a few things up online, and that probably didn't help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.81,
      "end_seconds": 272.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 274.52,
      "end_seconds": 285.36,
      "duration_seconds": 10.84,
      "text": "I swim twice a week. I'm vegetarian and have been for years. My husband and I live above the shop"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.71,
      "end_seconds": 298.32,
      "duration_seconds": 11.61,
      "text": "Right, here's what I'm thinking. The most likely explanation is constipation, possibly related to diet or medicines. I'd also keep low fibre intake in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 299.05,
      "end_seconds": 300.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.69,
      "end_seconds": 315.49,
      "duration_seconds": 13.8,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like constipation, possibly related to diet or medicines, but I'd like to confirm. Let's book a blood count to look into constipation."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 318.14,
      "end_seconds": 319.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "Does it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.57,
      "end_seconds": 356.92,
      "duration_seconds": 36.35,
      "text": "we should do blood tests for constipation i'm prescribing macrogol, 1 sachet, once a day, for two weeks that should help with constipation more fibre, plenty of water and and a regular time on the toilet after breakfast please don't wait if you are unable to pass wind or have severe tummy pain that's when to be seen urgently see me again in three weeks that's everything on my side anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 361.65,
      "end_seconds": 367.25,
      "duration_seconds": 5.6,
      "text": "right, you know, I'll do that. Thank you, doctor"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 368.79,
      "end_seconds": 370.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
